.TH DIRTOO 1 "August 2026" "dirtoo 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dirtoo \- modular Qt6 graphical file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dirtoo
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIPATH\fR|\fIURL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dirtoo
is a modular graphical file manager built with Qt6 and C++23.
It supports detail, icon, and list views, a filter expression language,
recursive search, thumbnails, read-only archive browsing, bookmarks,
location history, and clipboard-based copy/move operations.
.PP
If
.I PATH
or a
.I URL
is given, that location is opened on startup. Archive locations use the
form
.IR file:///path/to.zip//archive
or
.IR file:///path/to.zip//archive:entry .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable informational log messages on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug-level log messages (very verbose).
.SH VIEWS
.TP
.B Icons
Large icon grid with optional multi-line captions and media badges.
.TP
.B List
Windows 95-style list: small icon left of the filename, multi-column.
.TP
.B Detail
Tabular view with configurable columns (size, dimensions, aspect, FPS,
duration, modified, type, and optional width/height).
.SH FILTER EXPRESSIONS
The filter bar accepts a small DSL, for example:
.PP
.nf
  *.png
  size:>1M type:file
  contains:hello
.fi
.PP
See the in-app filter help for the full language.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dirtoo/dirtoo.conf
Application settings (view mode, zoom, columns, size units, …).
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/dirtoo-*
Archive extraction and thumbnail helper caches.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.TQ
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
.TQ
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Standard base directories for config, cache, and state data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dirtoo (1),
.BR dt-copy (1),
.BR dt-move (1),
.BR dt-rename (1),
.BR dt-rm (1),
.BR dt-mkdir (1),
